  m_Name: 1200
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Life Before Colonization Pre-14th Century
  info: Singapore, then known as "Temasek" or "Sea Town," thrives as a trading hub
    in the Malay Archipelago. Its strategic location near the Strait of Malacca makes
    it a vital stop for Chinese, Indian, and Arab merchants. The island's indigenous
    inhabitants, including the Orang Laut or "Sea People," play a critical role as
    skilled navigators and intermediaries in trade. Temasek is surrounded by dense
    jungles and swamps, with settlements primarily clustered near the coast.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 88baf38a697df4a01a0ace0cf81a7f9e, type: 3}
